{"type": "thinking", "text": "Check Date gaps:\n\n1. From 1981-02-14 18:32:00 to 2026-05-03 14:49:09. Let's compute.\nFrom 1981-02-14 to 2026-02-14 = 45 years. Then 2026-02-14 to 2026-05-03: Feb 14 → Mar 14 = 28 days (2026 not leap), Mar 14 → Apr 14 = 31 days, Apr 14 → May 3 = 19 days. Total = 28+31+19 = 78 days = 2 months 19 days (approx; calendar period). So 45 y 2 mo 19 d. Time: 18:32:00 → 14:49:09 next day? Actually 18:32 to 14:49:09 is 20h17m9s (from 18:32 to 14:49 next day = 20:17:09). The app shows \"45 y 2 mo 19 d 20 h 17 min 9 s\". That matches if months counted as 2 and days 19 with time 20:17:09. Good.\n\nBut wait, \"calendar periods computed directly up to the end timestamp\" - need to check whether it's correct. 45y 2mo 19d: 1981-02-14 + 45y = 2026-02-14; +2mo = 2026-04-14; +19d = 2026-05-03. Then time from 18:32:00 to 14:49:09 = 20h17m9s. Yes correct.\n\n2. 2020-03-10 22:15:00 to 2024-08-25 09:40:30. 2020-03-10 + 4y = 2024-03-10; +5mo = 2024-08-10; +15d = 2024-08-25. Time 22:15 → 09:40:30 = 11h25m30s. App shows 4y5mo15d11h25m30s ✓.\n\n3. date(2024,1,1) to date(2024,1,8) = 7 days = 1 week. App shows \"1 wk\" ✓. Hmm, \"1 wk\" only, not \"1 wk 0 d\". That's likely fine formatting.\n\nNow let's test Date gaps edge cases. Use scratchpad to test:\n- datetime(2024,1,31) to datetime(2024,2,29) — leap year\n- date(2024,3,1) to date(2024,2,29)? \n- datetime across DST? probably not.\n- reversed order: later to earlier → negative?\n\nThe changed in this build: \"Date range calculations: calendar periods are now computed directly up to the end timestamp.\" Potential bug: end-of-month handling. E.g., date(2024,1,31) to date(2024,3,1): If adding months naively: Jan 31 +1mo = Feb 31 invalid → Feb 29 (clamp), then +1 day = Mar 1 → \"1 mo 1 d\". Correct calendar difference is 1 month 1 day? Jan 31 to Mar 1 = 30 days (2024 leap: Jan31→Feb29 = 29 days, Feb29→Mar1 = 1 day) = 1 month 1 day. OK.\n\nPotential bug in \"computed directly up to the end timestamp\": maybe time fields wrong for certain cases. Let's test:\n- date(2024,1,1) to datetime(2024,1,2,12,0,0): expected \"1 d 12 h\"? Actually datetime to date conversion maybe treats date at midnight.\n- Negative/reverse.\n\nLet me also check the Date gaps results more deeply with a scratchpad.\n\nActually I should prioritize the 9 files and the changed areas. Let me test a few edge cases in scratchpad for dates, since date range calc changed.\n\nFirst, let me record: Date gaps current results all correct.\n\nLet me go to scratchpad and test:\n1. date(2024, 1, 31) to date(2024, 3, 1) → expect 1 mo 1 d\n2. datetime(2024, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0) to datetime(2024, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0) → 1 h\n3. date(2023, 3, 1) to date(2024, 2, 29) → 11 mo 28 d? Let's compute: 2023-03-01 + 11mo = 2024-02-01; +28d = 2024-02-29. Yes 11 mo 28 d.\n4. date(2024, 2, 29) to date(2025, 2, 28) → 1 y? 2024-02-29 + 1y = 2025-02-28 (clamp) → 0 d. Could display 1 y. Or 11 mo 30 d? Depends.\n\nLet me test in scratchpad. Press Back then scratchpad.\n\nActually I'm on Date gaps. Press Back to home, then tap scratchpad FAB."}
