fference 1 → 23h (correct). That's the borrow case and it worked. What about end time-of-day < start and end day < start day? E.g., datetime(2024,1,31,23,0,0) to datetime(2024,2,1,1,0,0) = 2h. Let's test. Could be a bug with month/day borrow. Also datetime(2024,3,31,23,0,0) to datetime(2024,4,1,1,0,0) = 2h. Hmm.\n\nLet me test datetime(2024,1,31,23,0,0) to datetime(2024,2,1,1,0,0). Expected 2h. If the algorithm adds 1 month to Jan 31 = Feb 29 > end, then 0 months, days = 1, time = -22h → borrow? Could produce \"1 d -22 h\" or \"2 h\". Let's see.\n\nAlso datetime(2024,1,31,10,0,0) to datetime(2024,2,29,9,0,0) = 28d23h? Jan31→Feb29 = 29 days minus 1h = 28d23h. Let's test.\n\nAnd datetime(2024,1,31,10,0,0) to datetime(2024,3,1,9,0,0). Days: Jan31→Mar1 = 30 days (leap), minus 1h = 29d23h. Month: Jan31+1mo=Feb29, +1d=Mar1, time -1h? Hmm.\n\nLet me test the tricky month-end case where day-of-month > end day-of-month and time borrow. E.g., datetime(2024,1,31,23,0,0) to datetime(2024,2,1,1,0,0).\n\nLet me do these in scratchpad. I need to add lines; earlier pressing ENTER created a new line and I can type into it via the focused field (no element arg). Let me try: press ENTER to create line, then type_text without element (types into focused field). Earlier I passed element 40 and it failed; maybe because tapping element 40 shifted. Let me instead use type_text without element while line 2 focused.\n\nActually the current state: line 1 \"32 fahrenheit in kelvin\". We might have lost line 2. Let me just clear and reuse line 1. It's simpler: long press select all, type. Ugh but reliable.\n\nAlternatively, create a new line by tapping at the blank area below line 1? The editor line 2 might still exist but empty. Actually the observe showed no line 2 element, so maybe empty lines are not shown (only lines with content or focused?). Hmm, the earlier Monthly budget file showed an empty EditText line 4 (element 10) and empty result. So empty lines are shown when they exist. In scratchpad, the new empty line 2 disappeared after typing? \n\nWait, in the last observation, elements 37 (line1 field), 38 (line1 result), then 39 \"2\"?? No, let me re-read: after pressing ENTER, elements: [36] \"1\", [37] EditText \"32 fahrenheit in kelvin\", [38] 273.15 K, [39] \"2\", [40] EditText (focused). Then after type_text element 40: elements [37] \"1\", [38] EditText \"32 fahrenheit in kelvin\" (focused), [39] 273.15 K, [40] Back. So line 2 vanished entirely, and line 1 became focused. The typed text \"1 kelvin in fahrenheit\" is gone! That's weird. Perhaps type_text tapped at (415,393) which was line 2, but the act of tapping outside line 1 committed line 1, and because line 2 was empty it was removed, and focus returned to line 1; then the text got typed... into line 1? But line 1 text unchanged.\n\nHmm, maybe the text \"1 kelvin in fahrenheit\" was typed but the app removed line 2 because it was invalid? No.\n\nActually maybe the type_text typed into line 2, then the app computed line 2 = \"1 kelvin in fahrenheit\" = -457.87°F, but then since scratchpad had only... no.\n\nThis is a rabbit hole. Let me just use line 1 via select-all.\n\nLet me do a series of tests with line 1. Each takes ~3 calls. Test 1: \"datetime(2024, 1, 31, 23, 0, 0) to datetime(2024, 2, 1, 1, 0, 0)\".\n\nLet me long press line 1 field (element 38)."}
