{"type": "thinking", "text": "\"that one is already logged.\" So the temperature bug is acknowledged/logged (probably from a previous report or the system knows). Good. So temperature bug is a known issue, logged. We don't need another. \n\nWait, \"already logged\" might mean my earlier report was actually logged despite \"could not reproduce\"? Or the bug is known. Either way, it's logged.\n\nSo confirmed bugs:\n1. Number bases scaling (confirmed & logged).\n2. Date gaps day borrow (confirmed & logged).\n3. Temperature arithmetic RHS unit (already logged).\n\nRemaining area: home screen file list. We tested search, sort, file info, relaunch, background load. Maybe there's a bug there too. Let me think about what \"files are now loaded in the background when the app launches\" could break.\n\nPossibilities:\n- On launch, a loading spinner then files appear; maybe the list flickers or briefly shows \"No files\". Hard to test.\n- Maybe there's a race where the pinned files or the sort order is applied incorrectly until reload.\n- Maybe after a file is modified and user returns via Back, the list doesn't refresh (we saw it did).\n- Maybe after deleting/duplicating, the list doesn't refresh.\n\nLet me test duplicate + delete to exercise list refresh. That's within the home file list area.\n\nActually, maybe the bug is: when the app launches, the file list is loaded in background, but the \"What's New\" or search bar is usable before load; if you tap search immediately, results are from stale/empty list. Hard.\n\nOr maybe the bug: the list loads only when the home screen is first shown, but if the app is launched directly into a file (e.g., \"open last file on launch\" setting), the home list is never loaded and shows empty when returning. We could test by enabling \"open last file on launch\" in Settings > Home & startup, then kill/relaunch (it opens last file), then go home and see if list loads. That's a plausible background-loading bug: the home list is loaded in the background only on launch, but if the app opens directly into a file, the list may be empty until refresh. Hmm! That's a good candidate.\n\nBut changing settings modifies app state. Could revert. Let me check Settings > Home & startup options. Maybe \"launch mode\". Let's inspect.\n\nActually, the changed note \"files are now loaded in the background when the app launches\" might mean the home screen loads files asynchronously. A bug could be that the list is empty if you return to home before load finishes. But on a fast device, hard to catch.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the bug is that the background load doesn't populate the \"file count\" used in search or sort until... no.\n\nLet me test duplicate and delete. It's straightforward and might reveal a refresh bug.\n\nPlan:\n1. From scratchpad, exit to home.\n2. Tap More options on Expenses (or any), choose Duplicate. Check a \"copy\" appears in the list (after background load/refresh).\n3. Then delete the copy via its More options > Delete, confirm. Check it's gone.\n\nThis exercises file list refresh. If duplicate doesn't appear until relaunch, bug. Let's do it.\n\nLet me exit scratchpad: BACK to dismiss keyboard, then Back app.\n\nActually the scratchpad currently has keyboard? After typing, keyboard is up. Press BACK then tap Back."}
