{"type": "text", "text": "The QA sweep is complete and the session has been signed off. Here's the summary:\n\n## Bugs found and logged\n\n1. **Number base conversions multiply the input by its radix** (confirmed & logged)\n   - `15 dec in hex` → `0x96` (150) instead of `0xF`\n   - `10 dec in bin` → `0b1100100` (100) instead of `0b1010`\n   - `64 dec in oct` → `0o1200` (640) instead of `0o100`\n   - `255 dec in hex` → `0x9F6` (2550) instead of `0xFF`\n   - Same on input: `15 hex in dec` → `240` instead of `21`\n\n2. **Date gaps fails to borrow a day when the end clock time is earlier** (confirmed & logged)\n   - `datetime(1981,2,14,18:32) → datetime(2026,5,3,14:49:09)` shows `45 y 2 mo 19 d 20 h 17 min 9 s` (should be 18 d — adding it lands one day past the end)\n   - `datetime(2024,1,1,12:00) → datetime(2024,2,1,11:00)` shows `1 mo 23 h` (should be 30 d 23 h; moving the end 1 h earlier *increased* the gap)\n\n3. **Temperature arithmetic uses Celsius instead of the right-hand unit** (already logged)\n   - `10 celsius + 18 fahrenheit` → `2.22 °C` instead of `68 °F`\n   - Documented example `35 °C + 10 degF in degF` → `73 °F` instead of `105 °F`\n\n4. **Cross-timezone `datetimeZ ... to ...` intervals ignore the end timezone** (already logged)\n   - Two datetimes representing the same instant show `5 h 30 min` instead of `0`\n   - Two datetimes 5.5 h apart show `0 d`\n\n## Areas verified clean\n- All 9 files present and complete; newest-first ordering, search, sort (Name / Date modified / Date created, both directions), duplicate, delete, New Calculation, File info, relaunch/background load, auto-open launch, and rotation.\n- Temperature *conversions* (C↔F↔K), generic length conversions, Expenses, Monthly budget, Remainders, Percentages, Time differences, and the documented date `between`/`to` operators."}
